  "why": "FileHashHelper.ReadLast32Bytes and ComputeMd5WithoutLast32Bytes exist in both PC Tool builds, but their only caller is the developer menu item MainFrm.读img中的md5ToolStripMenuItem_Click, hard-coded to D:\\\\1\\\\vrx_pro+max+cine\\\\Ascent_VRX_Pro_17_5_3.img. The production upgrade path validates no image content at all. This fixture establishes what that vendor scheme actually describes: it holds for every RKFW receiver image and for none of the ASW air/ground images -- which is why this project reports the result and never gates on it.",
  "field_meanings": {
    "md5_whole_file": "MD5 of the ENTIRE file. This is the value FileTransferSession.ComputeMD5 puts into ArFileInfo.MD5 and the device verifies (CompareMD5).",
    "md5_of_body": "MD5 over the file MINUS its last 32 bytes -- ComputeMd5WithoutLast32Bytes.",
    "trailing_md5_declared": "the last 32 bytes read as ASCII, when they are 32 hex characters.",
    "asw_header": "ASW container header: magic, u32BoardType, u32SdkVersion, u32AppVersion, u32QaVersion, per ar_fpvhs_upgrade’s own log format. Advisory only.",
    "distributed_in_zip": "the image arrived inside an archive. The archive is a distribution wrapper; the PC Tool never opens one -- its file dialog filter is *.img and UpgradeProcessFSM.Start() opens the .img directly."
  },
